<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20961] FLR-ECRO: data_version blocks on EC file with unavailable OST</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20961</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lfs data_version&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;LL_IOC_DATA_VERSION&lt;/tt&gt;) on an EC file with a data stripe on an unavailable OST blocks until the OST returns, so &lt;tt&gt;lfs mirror resync&lt;/tt&gt;/&lt;tt&gt;verify&lt;/tt&gt;, HSM archive and &lt;tt&gt;lfs migrate&lt;/tt&gt; of an otherwise readable file hang.  See the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20212" title="FLR-ECRO: verify non-write RPCs do not block client " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20212"&gt;LU-20212&lt;/a&gt; test results.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;osc_io_data_version_end &amp;lt; cl_io_end &amp;lt; lov_io_end_wrapper &amp;lt; lov_io_data_version_end &amp;lt; cl_io_end &amp;lt; cl_io_loop &amp;lt; ll_ioc_data_version &amp;lt; ll_file_ioctl
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;66567 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20212" title="FLR-ECRO: verify non-write RPCs do not block client " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20212"&gt;LU-20212&lt;/a&gt;) only fails fast for a deactivated import.  For a file in RDONLY state the objects cannot change while the layout lock is held, so the version could be taken without the unavailable object, or the RPC could at least be sent no-delay and fail with an error the tools can handle.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
